Upstream bug: /key/delete evicts the deleted keys only from the handling
worker's auth cache. Every other worker, and in apps/litellm-stack.yml the
gateway, keeps authenticating a deleted key from its cached copy until
user_api_key_cache_ttl (60 s) expires, while /key/block and /key/update reach
every worker through the coordination Redis.

https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/47609
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/45296

Backport the /key/delete part of #47609: evict the deleted rows through
delete_cache_key_objects, which removes them locally, from Redis, and from
every other worker over the auth cache invalidation channel.

Removal check: tests/verify_key_delete.py

diff --git a/litellm/proxy/management_endpoints/key_management_endpoints.py b/litellm/proxy/management_endpoints/key_management_endpoints.py
